# @ryph/model-proxy — environment for the PROXY composition root (`bun run dev`): the
# data-plane process agent containers dial as their "provider". The management surface (key
# CRUD, virtual-key minting) is NOT served here — it mounts into the control plane; the shared
# database is the seam between the two processes.
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and adjust.

# ── Listener ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#RYPH_MODEL_PROXY_PORT=7420

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED: the AES-GCM master key unsealing provider keys — the same 64-hex-char value the
# control plane seals them with (RYPH_SECRETS_KEY there).
#RYPH_SECRETS_KEY=

# ── Database ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A ryph database URL: pglite:<path>, pglite:memory:// or postgres://… . Normally the CONTROL
# PLANE's database, where keys and virtual keys are written — point this at the same value.
# Note that a pglite path opened by two PROCESSES diverges silently, so sharing one that way
# needs a postgres:// server; a single process sharing one connection is the supported shape.
#RYPH_DB=pglite:./data/ryph

# ── Custom model endpoints ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set to 1 to let an admin register a model endpoint at a loopback, link-local or private-range
# address — a LAN vLLM, and nothing else. Plain http is permitted only for such an address, so
# this never becomes "the sealed key may cross the public internet in cleartext". Off, a base URL
# must be https and must not literally name an address the deployment answers on. The pod's
# NetworkPolicy excepts every private range regardless; this only moves the registration check.
#RYPH_ALLOW_PRIVATE_MODEL_ENDPOINTS=1

# ── Logging ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# debug / info / warn / error / critical.
#RYPH_LOG_LEVEL=info
# json / text / colorful (default depends on whether stdout is a tty).
#RYPH_LOG_FORMAT=
